Z||000003||Fierobruiser||11-22-2001||11:59 AM||||I've only done this in small sections as a touch-up for a very sloppy paint job where the owner missed sections and the primer was still showing. I cleaned the surface, painted the small areas (largest was about 6"x6") with Duplicolor, did a little polishing, buffing to blend and then topped off with spray clear coat, It looks good, hardly noticeable on the black. You could just clean the areas, mask and spray from a can. It'd have to be an improvement without a whole lot of effort if your springing for a pro paint job in the Spring. Tell me how you post pics. I haven't been able to figure it out yet.<P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Spektrum-87GT||11-22-2001||12:32 PM||||just use [ img ]http://www.host.com/folder/image.jpg [ /img ]<P><BR>WITHOUT THE SPACES!!! so its like [img ]... but without that second space too. [test] like that.<BR>you've gotta have a place to host your pics too... thats a completely different animal, hope that helps!||||reg||1
Z||000005||REDHOTT88||11-22-2001||12:40 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR>[B]i'm getting a new paint job next spring, but is there anything i can do to help this paint out a little bit? it looks plain terrible during the day<P>Looks like your clearcoat is peeled, now the paint has lost its pigments. You can rub and polish all you want, even buy all the compounds and colorback products you want and it wont change much..<P>Time for a professional paint job! Sorry.<BR><P>------------------<BR>1988 Formula (red & shiny allover)- and she doesn't like to wear a bra!<BR>1st Place IMOMOC (In My Own Mind Of Course!)<BR>2nd Place IMWM (In My Wifes Mind!)||||reg||1
